Install:
- PostgreSQL - SQL Engine that stores data and reads queries and return information.
- PgAdmin - Graphical User Interface for connecting with PostgreSQL

Steps to Install postgres:
- https://www.postgresql.org/download/
    - Click "Download the installer"
- Click and proceed.(uncheck stack builders)

Steps to Install PgAdmin
- https://www.pgadmin.org/download/
Note: This will get already installed when you install postgresql.

Open PgAdmin > Select server > Select Database
- Create Database called "rentaldvd" by right clicking "Databases".
- Right click the "rentaldvd" database and select "restore" and select the "dvdrental.tar" file.
    - Before restore switch pre/post & Data option.
- Right click & select "Query Tool" and write you Query
    - SELECT * FROM film;
